# Thank You Girl, intro: the neighbor-tone embellishment of the A and G chords (figure 16.2)
# Each typed pair ("E-E-") is two eighths. Over A, the top E steps up to its neighbor F# on beats 2
# and 4 while C# and A sound on 1 and 3; over G, the top D steps up to E on 2 and 4 over B and G.
# Pollack draws the top notes on two rows as a little pitch graph; they are one line here.
# The chord row (A, G) is added from fig. 16.1; Pollack types only the notes.
#? The second note of each upper pair is typed "F-", read as F# (the same neighbor as "F#-");
#? check whether it is really an F-natural.
#? Octaves (A3 up to F#4) are a guess at the guitar/harmonica register.
key D

